# Virtual environment and interpreter caches
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Tool caches
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Coverage output
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
/htmlcov/

# Build artefacts. Anchored with a leading slash: without it, a trailing-slash
# pattern matches a directory of that name at any depth, and `build/` silently
# excluded src/commissura/build/ from version control for three commits.
# Every plain directory name below is anchored for the same reason.
/dist/
/build/
*.egg-info/

# Pseudonymisation keys. Never commit one: the whole design rests on the key
# staying outside the dataset, and a key in a repository is a key in every
# clone, every fork and every mirror, permanently.
*.key
*.pem

# Generated corpora and datasets. Reproducible from a seed, so committing them
# adds weight without adding information — and a raw corpus deliberately
# contains synthetic identifiers, which do not belong in version control even
# when they are fake.
/raw/
/dataset/
/corpus/

# Downloaded reference material (specifications, authority lists). Someone
# else's documents, fetched on demand and recorded by URL in CLAUDE.md.
/reference/

# Editor and OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Audit and remediation paperwork, kept out of the repository on purpose.
# These described the findings of 2026-11-13 with working reproduction steps,
# which is a recipe against any dataset built before they were fixed. They are
# listed here and not merely deleted because `git add -A` is how two of them
# got committed in the first place, in a commit whose message did not mention
# them. The decisions they recorded live in CLAUDE.md's log, which is where
# this project keeps decisions; the reproductions do not need a home here.
/SECURITY_AUDIT.md
/ENGINEERING_REVIEW.md
/REMEDIATION_REPORT.md
/IDENTITY_RESOLUTION.md
/HARDENING_CHANGELOG.md
